From u3edc58ee737edd94 at groups.google.com  Sat Dec 10 20:24:21 2016
From: u3edc58ee737edd94 at groups.google.com (Stefan Th. Gries)
Date: Sat, 10 Dec 2016 20:24:21 +0000
Subject: Re: [CorpLing with R] Adding horizontal lines to 3d scatterplot
Message-ID: <CpHmvMd7ErU.Nnfp_vieDwAJ@corpling-with-r.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <CpHmvMd7ErU.ogaQa9SEDwAJ@corpling-with-r.groups.google.com>
References: <CpHmvMd7ErU.ogaQa9SEDwAJ@corpling-with-r.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/corpling-with-r/c/CpHmvMd7ErU/m/Nnfp_vieDwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

See <https://www.jstatsoft.org/index.php/jss/article/view/v008i11/JSSs3d.pdf>, Section 3. That means for your case:

library(scatterplot3d)
dat <- data.frame(x=c(rep(1:4,16)),
                  y=c(rep(c(rep(1,4),rep(2,4),rep(3,4),rep(4,4)),4)),
                  z=c(rep(1,16),rep(2,16),rep(3,16),rep(4,16)))
qwe <- scatterplot3d(dat, type="h", color="blue")
qwe$points3d(c(1.5,1.5,1.5), c(2.5,2.5,2.5),type="b",col="red",cex=3,pch=16)

Best,
STG
